WEBVTT

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:03.711
Cash, cash,
cash for your bones!

00:00:03.896 --> 00:00:06.814
Too many bones? Not enough
cash? Call Cash Bone!

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:09.567
Ribs, skulls, spines,
even certain tiny ear bones.

00:00:09.651 --> 00:00:12.153
The leg bone's connected to the Cash Bone!

00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:49.482
Aw! Nibbler made
a bobo for Mama.

00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:52.902
I'll pick it up with my
supey-dupey poopy scoopy.

00:01:03.831 --> 00:01:06.541
Core magnetic field,
31 microteslas.

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:07.750
Nice.

00:01:07.876 --> 00:01:09.961
Temperature? Whoa!

00:01:10.045 --> 00:01:12.922
The magma P. I. is 10,000 degrees Selleck!

00:01:17.052 --> 00:01:18.928
Leela, I am
collecting data.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.555
Could you dump that
somewhere else?

00:01:20.639 --> 00:01:25.101
Not really. It's highly volatile
dark matter and some corn.

00:01:25.269 --> 00:01:27.311
But I'm presenting
my thesis tomorrow,

00:01:27.396 --> 00:01:29.522
and I've barely
had time to prepare.

00:01:29.606 --> 00:01:33.693
Nonsense. You've been my
grad student for 12 years.

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:35.278
You were ready
six years ago.

00:01:35.362 --> 00:01:36.362
What?

00:01:36.446 --> 00:01:38.447
I probably
should have told you.

00:01:38.532 --> 00:01:41.868
Anyway, the important thing
is to be relaxed tomorrow.

00:01:41.952 --> 00:01:42.952
Are you sure?

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.036
Yes.

00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:46.539
Do what you young
people do to unwind.

00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:48.791
Take a joyride
in your jalopy.

00:01:48.876 --> 00:01:52.378
Wear a T-shirt and eat a fish stick. Go!

00:01:59.177 --> 00:02:03.306
Okay, amigos, one teensy drink to help Amy relax.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.557
Hear, hear!

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.228
Hmm.

00:02:09.313 --> 00:02:11.272
I guess I'm still
kind of nervous.

00:02:11.356 --> 00:02:14.317
One more teensy drink
to help Amy relax.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.697
Still a little
nervous?

00:02:20.824 --> 00:02:22.241
She's a nervous wreck!

00:02:39.301 --> 00:02:41.344
Well, I may not
have a man,

00:02:41.428 --> 00:02:43.846
but at least I've got you, poopsie-doodle.

00:02:46.516 --> 00:02:49.936
Leela, it's time
you and I had a talk.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.356
A talk? You can't break up
with me. You're my pet!

00:02:53.482 --> 00:02:57.276
As much as I enjoy being the
object of your misplaced affections,

00:02:57.361 --> 00:02:59.278
I am also a highly
sophisticated being

00:02:59.363 --> 00:03:01.864
who longs for intelligent conversation.

00:03:02.032 --> 00:03:05.201
Aw! Is shnookums not feeling shtimuwated?

00:03:05.369 --> 00:03:07.286
An understatement,
to say the least.

00:03:07.371 --> 00:03:09.622
It's time you treated me with respect.

00:03:09.915 --> 00:03:12.917
If you want to be treated like
a fellow crew member, fine,

00:03:13.001 --> 00:03:14.627
but no more
purse rides,

00:03:14.711 --> 00:03:17.630
and no more dressing you up in
your cute little sailor suit.

00:03:17.714 --> 00:03:20.716
I keep telling you that's my real naval uniform.

00:03:23.762 --> 00:03:25.137
Your place or mine?

00:03:25.222 --> 00:03:27.807
Both. But first,
this place.

00:03:31.186 --> 00:03:34.355
Ooh! Room for one more?

00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:44.407
I thought
I set you for 7:15!

00:03:44.574 --> 00:03:47.368
Sorry, I hooked up with Bender last night.

00:03:47.452 --> 00:03:49.829
Dude was all over
my snooze button.

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:54.250
But my doctoral exam
is in 10 minutes. On Mars!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.963
Ew! Kif, did you
yack on the floor?

00:03:59.256 --> 00:04:01.257
Yes, I did.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.393
Where's your candidate,
Farnsworth?

00:04:12.519 --> 00:04:15.021
I have a long list of students to humiliate today.

00:04:18.108 --> 00:04:19.525
You're late,
Miss Wong.

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:23.029
Oh, God, this is like
one of those nightmares!

00:04:24.239 --> 00:04:26.282
Here, take my lab coat.

00:04:27.409 --> 00:04:29.660
Allow me to introduce
your examining committee

00:04:29.745 --> 00:04:31.746
in descending order
of grumpiness.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.081
Professor
Ogden Wernstrom.

00:04:34.166 --> 00:04:35.374
Wernstrom.

00:04:35.459 --> 00:04:39.211
Downtown Professor of Applied
Physics, Ethan "Bubblegum" Tate.

00:04:39.296 --> 00:04:43.007
I see by your curriculum vitae
that you're a Sagittarius.

00:04:43.091 --> 00:04:45.760
And Professor
Fisherprice Shpeekenshpell.

00:04:46.511 --> 00:04:47.887
The cow says...

00:04:49.306 --> 00:04:53.601
He proved that 50 years ago, and
he's been coasting on it ever since.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:58.439
I am the esteemed Professor Morris
Katz, and you are wasting my time.

00:04:58.565 --> 00:04:59.648
Proceed.

00:05:00.859 --> 00:05:02.234
Imagine,
if you will...

00:05:02.319 --> 00:05:03.277
Oh, God.

00:05:03.361 --> 00:05:07.907
A gigantic spherical generator, one
that could provide unlimited energy

00:05:07.991 --> 00:05:10.409
because it's essentially
in perpetual motion.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.788
Young lady, have you been drinking?

00:05:13.997 --> 00:05:16.665
Well, yes,
but that's not revelant.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.586
I'm talking about Earth.
Earth's the generator.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:25.174
Suppose this basketball
is the whole world.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:28.385
To many young men
in the inner city, it is.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:32.014
As it spins, it's producing
an enormous magnetic field.

00:05:32.099 --> 00:05:35.226
If we could use that field
to generate electric current,

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:40.189
we could actually harness the
Earth's rotational ener... Ener...

00:05:40.315 --> 00:05:43.192
Yes, tapping the Earth's ener-kerchoo.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:44.276
Go on.

00:05:44.528 --> 00:05:46.779
Sorry, I'm super-allergic to cats.

00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:48.781
Professor Katz,
would you mind...

00:05:48.865 --> 00:05:50.699
Miss Wong,
I mind everything.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:58.040
You just need to polarize the
Earth's core with a huge static charge

00:05:58.959 --> 00:06:01.877
by ratcheting superconducting wire down into...

00:06:02.003 --> 00:06:04.004
Sorry.

00:06:04.589 --> 00:06:07.883
Enough. The committee members
will now vote yea or nay.

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:09.677
Nay.
Nay.

00:06:09.761 --> 00:06:11.095
Hell, nay.

00:06:11.888 --> 00:06:15.057
The horse says,
"Doctorate denied".

00:06:25.235 --> 00:06:26.485
It's okay, Amy.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.362
I don't have
a fancy degree either,

00:06:28.446 --> 00:06:32.241
but today I'm a prominent boy
in the package delivery field.

00:06:38.582 --> 00:06:41.458
Now that I am a full
and equal member of the crew,

00:06:41.543 --> 00:06:44.336
I pledge my loyalty,
my perspicacity

00:06:44.421 --> 00:06:47.131
and, dare I say it,
my friendship.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.008
Leela, muzzle
that skunk.

00:06:49.092 --> 00:06:51.427
We can't stop a meeting for
some cute, fuzzy, little...

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.429
Hey,
look, a kitty cat.

00:06:54.598 --> 00:06:55.681
You again?

00:06:55.765 --> 00:06:59.268
Get away,
you mangy ball of histamines.

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:00.936
You leave
kitty cat alone!

00:07:01.062 --> 00:07:02.980
Kitty cat.

00:07:03.064 --> 00:07:06.025
People, please, I'm trying to run a business,

00:07:06.109 --> 00:07:08.194
so I get to hold kitty.
Here, puss, puss...

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.112
No, me. Over here. I wanna hold him.

00:07:10.822 --> 00:07:13.115
Its anus looks
like an asterisk.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.207
Captain Fuzzy Toes reporting
for duty. I mean, cutie.

00:07:23.585 --> 00:07:26.128
My best friend died
in that uniform.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:27.463
I hate that cat!

00:07:27.881 --> 00:07:31.217
If I had a spray bottle,
I'd give him such a spritzing.

00:07:31.301 --> 00:07:32.635
I'll tell you one thing,

00:07:32.719 --> 00:07:36.013
nothing acts that cute
without some ulterior motive.

00:07:39.476 --> 00:07:42.102
Aw! You want
your dipey changed?

00:07:44.231 --> 00:07:46.732
We'll have to watch
its every move.

00:07:47.943 --> 00:07:49.235
Powder, please.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:13.842
Here's my new theory:
That is one adorable cat.

00:08:13.969 --> 00:08:16.053
I guess
I was just jealous.

00:08:16.263 --> 00:08:18.347
I do miss being
Leela's shnookums.

00:08:18.807 --> 00:08:21.725
I'm going to apologize
and hope for a pity pet.

00:08:23.061 --> 00:08:24.228
Yes, my lord.

00:08:24.521 --> 00:08:26.772
Amy and Nibbler
are a tewwible thweat.

00:08:26.898 --> 00:08:29.692
They must be spayed
and neutered, wespectivewy.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:51.922
The cat is evil!
We have proof!

00:08:52.007 --> 00:08:53.340
It was summoning
a saucer.

00:08:53.425 --> 00:08:56.302
Of course it wanted a saucer, you idiot.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.221
A saucer of
dewicious cweam.

00:09:00.348 --> 00:09:02.725
You fool, this isn't
about the cream!

00:09:02.892 --> 00:09:05.477
It's pwonounced
"cweam"!

00:09:05.937 --> 00:09:08.147
I'm petting mine
down to the bone.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.191
Just stwoke
its fwuffy fur.

00:09:11.609 --> 00:09:13.694
Scwatch its fwubby chin.

00:09:13.945 --> 00:09:16.405
Fweeble its fwooby pwow.

00:09:16.906 --> 00:09:18.907
Pet it. Pet it.

00:09:19.075 --> 00:09:22.161
Pet it. Pet it.

00:09:22.245 --> 00:09:23.203
No, no!

00:09:23.288 --> 00:09:24.288
Pet it. Pet it.

00:09:24.372 --> 00:09:27.124
Pet it. Pet it.

00:09:37.927 --> 00:09:40.888
What do cats need with that much yarn and cobalt?

00:09:40.972 --> 00:09:44.433
They're doing something downstairs.
We've got to find out what.

00:09:46.144 --> 00:09:48.896
Where do you think
you're going, No-cat?

00:09:49.773 --> 00:09:52.483
The basement. I think I
left the air hockey table on.

00:09:52.567 --> 00:09:56.528
Without a cat,
you ain't going nowhere.

00:09:56.613 --> 00:09:58.864
Can you at least tell us
what's going on down there?

00:09:58.948 --> 00:10:01.700
We're certainly not building something sinister,

00:10:01.785 --> 00:10:03.285
if that's what
you're implying.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:07.122
Now, come on, Bender, something
sinister won't build itself.

00:10:11.002 --> 00:10:13.629
Professor Katz's
last name is Katz.

00:10:13.713 --> 00:10:16.090
Do you think he has something
to do with these cats?

00:10:16.174 --> 00:10:19.385
The conclusion is as inescapable as it is moronic.

00:10:19.469 --> 00:10:22.971
I say we pay him a visit,
and if he won't talk to us,

00:10:23.181 --> 00:10:24.890
he'll talk to
Smith &amp; Wesson

00:10:26.059 --> 00:10:28.602
or, perhaps,
Consolidated Head Melter.

00:10:49.582 --> 00:10:52.084
Professor Katz,
we want answers!

00:10:54.796 --> 00:10:58.715
I warn you, if I have to get
cute, it's gonna get ugly.

00:11:02.178 --> 00:11:04.304
He's dead!

00:11:04.389 --> 00:11:06.890
Wait. What are these
strings on his lap?

00:11:08.643 --> 00:11:10.936
What the...
He isn't dead.

00:11:11.271 --> 00:11:13.355
He's one of those
dog-operated puppets

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.524
that's been adapted
for use by a cat!

00:11:15.692 --> 00:11:18.819
So, I had my doctorate
denied by that fuzzball?

00:11:20.196 --> 00:11:21.238
Bad kitty!

00:11:41.092 --> 00:11:44.803
They actually built the
planetary ratchet from my thesis!

00:11:50.518 --> 00:11:51.518
Uh-oh!

00:11:52.395 --> 00:11:53.479
What the...

00:11:55.857 --> 00:11:58.817
Well, look what
the me dragged in.

00:11:59.068 --> 00:12:00.152
You can talk!

00:12:00.236 --> 00:12:01.487
You can talk?

00:12:01.571 --> 00:12:03.071
How ironic.

00:12:03.156 --> 00:12:07.659
Two hyper-intelligent beings both
pretending to be simple house pets.

00:12:07.744 --> 00:12:09.703
Say, do you know
Obliteron?

00:12:09.787 --> 00:12:12.206
He pretends to be
a hamster, but...

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:15.417
Yeah, that's really great. Could
you please tell us what's going on?

00:12:15.502 --> 00:12:17.252
What? Oh! Right.

00:12:17.545 --> 00:12:20.672
You see, my associates and I
are from the ninth planet

00:12:20.757 --> 00:12:22.674
of the star
you call Thuban.

00:12:22.759 --> 00:12:25.552
Long ago,
life there was ideal.

00:12:27.388 --> 00:12:30.140
The sun provided plenty of warm, dozy light.

00:12:30.391 --> 00:12:32.267
The chicken-salmon
roamed free.

00:12:34.229 --> 00:12:36.438
Yet disaster loomed.

00:12:36.773 --> 00:12:39.399
Our planet's rotation
was gradually slowing.

00:12:39.609 --> 00:12:41.527
At first,
it seemed beneficial.

00:12:41.611 --> 00:12:43.862
Long, dark nights
for sleeping,

00:12:43.947 --> 00:12:46.198
long, sunny days
for sleeping.

00:12:46.449 --> 00:12:48.325
But then it got too hot.

00:12:50.787 --> 00:12:51.995
And too cold.

00:12:55.208 --> 00:12:57.334
Our top scientists
went to work.

00:12:58.294 --> 00:13:01.547
At last, they located a planet
with the necessary orientation

00:13:01.631 --> 00:13:04.967
and magnetic field to
harness its rotational energy.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.886
Earth!
Indubitably.

00:13:07.971 --> 00:13:09.721
Although we call it
Blue Blue Shiny Ball.

00:13:16.604 --> 00:13:18.230
In the area
now known as Egypt,

00:13:18.314 --> 00:13:22.192
my people constructed a
giant, semi-octahedral antenna

00:13:22.277 --> 00:13:24.820
to beam Earth's rotational energy to Thuban.

00:13:24.904 --> 00:13:26.822
The Great
Pyramid at Giza!

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:30.325
Yes. The Egyptians
viewed us as gods,

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.078
but ironically,
that was our downfall.

00:13:33.621 --> 00:13:38.250
They pampered us with feasts most
fancy and victuals most tender.

00:13:38.668 --> 00:13:41.003
We grew fat
and domesticated.

00:13:42.672 --> 00:13:44.089
Thousands of years passed,

00:13:44.173 --> 00:13:47.175
and our home world was nearing total destruction.

00:13:51.973 --> 00:13:52.931
Shut up!

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.436
But the technology
to save our planet was lost.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.690
Lost, that is, until I heard
you speak at Mars University.

00:14:01.858 --> 00:14:05.736
So, you called my thesis a fat sack
of barf, and then you stole it?

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.195
Welcome to academia.

00:14:07.363 --> 00:14:10.574
He intends to siphon off
Earth's rotational energy!

00:14:10.658 --> 00:14:12.367
Earth will come
to a stop, and...

00:14:12.452 --> 00:14:15.329
Half of you will cook,
and half of you will freeze.

00:14:15.413 --> 00:14:20.125
Earth will be one big McDLT. We
just got that commercial last year.

00:14:20.209 --> 00:14:22.127
Oh, yeah, smarty paws?

00:14:22.211 --> 00:14:25.172
You may have built the ratchet,
but you can't reach the core

00:14:25.256 --> 00:14:28.175
without 4,000 miles
of superconducting wire.

00:14:28.343 --> 00:14:30.010
The ball of yarn!

00:14:37.268 --> 00:14:38.310
Quite.

00:14:38.394 --> 00:14:42.272
Even so, you'd still need a
tremendously powerful static charge

00:14:42.357 --> 00:14:43.607
to trigger the process.

00:14:43.691 --> 00:14:45.609
Ever had a cat
rub up against you?

00:14:45.693 --> 00:14:48.612
If you're propositioning me,
I'm not interested.

00:14:48.738 --> 00:14:50.614
I'm talking about
the charge generated

00:14:50.698 --> 00:14:54.993
when 50,000 felines rub against a single surface.

00:14:55.203 --> 00:14:56.578
Professor?

00:15:26.484 --> 00:15:28.777
Soon the world
will come to a stop,

00:15:28.861 --> 00:15:31.279
and there's nothing
you can do to stop it.

00:15:31.781 --> 00:15:34.991
The stopping of the world,
that is. It's unstoppable.

00:15:37.453 --> 00:15:38.453
Excuse me.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.590
The Earth is
coming to a stop!

00:15:50.675 --> 00:15:52.843
Keep your eyes on
the kitties and push!

00:15:56.806 --> 00:16:01.852
These space cats seem to be employing
some form of hypnotic hyper-cuteness.

00:16:01.978 --> 00:16:05.021
Well, two can play at that
game. And one of them is me.

00:16:08.359 --> 00:16:10.527
Nibbler? Poopsie-doodle?

00:16:12.488 --> 00:16:15.782
Mr. Winkles, Smudge-Smudge.
Quick, dance with each other!

00:16:18.661 --> 00:16:19.661
Aw!

00:16:19.996 --> 00:16:21.163
Aw!

00:16:21.247 --> 00:16:23.206
Damn, they are good.

00:16:27.003 --> 00:16:30.338
We're coming to a full stop.
All cats, to your posts!

00:16:42.435 --> 00:16:44.728
Catastrophe Beach Party.
Scene One.

00:16:45.062 --> 00:16:47.522
Cue disaster effects,
and action!

00:16:53.196 --> 00:16:56.740
Cut! That extra looked at the
camera. We'll have to do it again.

00:17:00.369 --> 00:17:03.455
And now to transfer your
planet's rotational energy

00:17:03.539 --> 00:17:04.664
to my home world.

00:17:21.682 --> 00:17:25.060
Well, now, this calls for a celebration.

00:17:35.196 --> 00:17:37.405
What's all this cat
hair on my sweater?

00:17:38.866 --> 00:17:42.327
Why am I full of sand?
And Tootsie Rolls?

00:17:42.411 --> 00:17:45.747
You were all under the spell
of those obnoxious space cats!

00:17:46.123 --> 00:17:48.875
Enjoy being broiled alive by the sun,

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.628
and also the dead bird
we've left in your slipper.

00:17:55.424 --> 00:17:57.926
Quickly! If we turn
the ratchet the other way,

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:00.428
perhaps we can
restart the Earth!

00:18:03.474 --> 00:18:06.309
It won't turn.
Push harder, Bender!

00:18:06.644 --> 00:18:09.437
I can't! You should have
called my cousin, Turner.

00:18:10.857 --> 00:18:12.858
It's hopeless.

00:18:12.942 --> 00:18:16.528
Even in theory, the device can
only apply force in one direction.

00:18:16.612 --> 00:18:19.573
Can someone open a window? It's
getting a little warm in here.

00:18:22.326 --> 00:18:23.910
Is that better?

00:18:31.752 --> 00:18:33.461
Shmeezus, it's hot!

00:18:33.546 --> 00:18:36.339
Why'd I have to invent
that awful device?

00:18:38.593 --> 00:18:42.429
Amy, technology isn't
intrinsically good or evil.

00:18:42.513 --> 00:18:45.640
It's how it's used.
Like the death ray.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.475
Maybe you're right.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.645
I guess science has to keep pushing
forward with the hope that...

00:18:50.813 --> 00:18:53.899
That's it!
Pushing forward!

00:18:53.983 --> 00:18:56.651
Professor, I know how
to restart the Earth!

00:18:56.777 --> 00:18:59.029
You can't
suddenly know something

00:18:59.113 --> 00:19:01.573
just by assembling
a committee of words.

00:19:01.657 --> 00:19:05.160
That's it!
I'll assemble your committee!

00:19:06.162 --> 00:19:07.829
The ratchet
won't turn backwards,

00:19:07.914 --> 00:19:10.123
but what if we kept
pushing it forward?

00:19:10.625 --> 00:19:12.584
Earth would start
turning again!

00:19:12.668 --> 00:19:14.836
Yes, the wrong direction!

00:19:17.006 --> 00:19:18.131
So?

00:19:19.508 --> 00:19:24.012
Gentlemen, ladies, let's get this globe trotting.

00:19:28.517 --> 00:19:31.561
It's working!
Just a little faster!

00:19:31.771 --> 00:19:33.313
But we're plotzing here!

00:19:33.522 --> 00:19:34.898
Then look at Nibbler!

00:19:39.153 --> 00:19:40.362
Aw!

00:19:52.083 --> 00:19:54.876
On the whole, Earth's society is worthless.

00:19:54.961 --> 00:19:56.836
But they do have
these things called

00:19:56.921 --> 00:19:59.589
antique rugs that are
great for peeing on.

00:20:12.687 --> 00:20:13.895
Good show.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:22.445
And though the world is now spinning in
the wrong direction, it's good enough.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.822
Well done, Amy.

00:20:23.906 --> 00:20:27.325
I'm honored to begrudgingly
present you with your Ph. D.

00:20:27.451 --> 00:20:29.077
in applied physics.

00:20:29.161 --> 00:20:33.289
Also, some kind of sportsmanship
award I had in my glove compartment.

00:20:33.499 --> 00:20:38.044
Yay! I'm finally done with
school! How's the job market?

00:20:38.671 --> 00:20:39.754
Rough.

00:20:39.839 --> 00:20:42.424
Congratulations,
Dr. Wong!

00:20:43.759 --> 00:20:45.343
Congratulations.

00:20:46.303 --> 00:20:48.179
Permission
to come aboard?

00:20:48.264 --> 00:20:50.098
Granted, shnookums.

00:20:58.107 --> 00:21:00.358
You've got
a bright future, Amy.

00:21:00.443 --> 00:21:03.528
As sure as the sun
sets in the east.